/obj/structure/tatarla_statue
	name = "\improper The Tatarla statue"
	desc = "Granite statue of Tatarla, each corner of the statue has hand-carved corners, incisions, multiple depressions and shapes. Some kind of energy emanates from this structure, as if you feel like dozens of craftsmen have ground hundreds of chisels on this stone, and shed thousands of drops of sweat to free Tatarla from a stone as powerful as its character. In his eyes, gray as this world, you can see an equally determined will that breaks through stone, like rays of light through the boundless darkness of space, and even the granite boundaries of stone sculptures are unable to stop, as if even death itself, this will and this tread, which is transmitted to everyone nearby... Socrates once said, "Whoever wants to move the world, let him move himself," and it is these words that come out through the stone molecules of the monument, the energy of calm and perseverance, like a frozen movement, like a caught look. The dew that fell, the lost moment, the raised sword, the blow, forward. At the bottom of the sculpture, various battle scenes are visible, an innumerable army of the so-called "UNG", led by the largest unga, a bearded Tatar warrior, galloping on horseback, dissecting the xenomorphic yoke with their sabers, and Jesus from above, for everything is good that is from God, and it cannot be bad that is from God, and like a host, the small UNG army, but magnanimous and fearless, rushes into the ranks of the hungry, crazed xenomorphic scum, who only longs for blood and death.  The Ungs are being slaughtered, there are more of them, but Tatarla gives them spirit. There are words written even below the monument, but they are no longer legible..."

	icon = 'icons/obj/structures/tatarla_statue.dmi'
	icon_state = 'tatarla_statue'
/obj/structure/tatarla_statue/Initialize(mapload)
	. = ..()
